Large experiment attempted, then fully reverted
- I attempted strict `MAT/SWI` scrutinee forcing in compiled code:
  - first with `aot_force_whnf()` calling `wnf()` directly,
  - then with `WNF_S_POS` sync,
  - then with APP-frame scrutinee writeback,
  - then with bounded ALO-only forcing via `wnf_alo_*`.
- All those variants caused AOT regressions (segfaults, `cannot apply a number`, wrong outputs, huge malformed terms in `enum_primes`, hangs/kills).
- Everything from that forcing experiment was reverted.
- Key lesson: strict-site forcing is very sensitive to stack/frame invariants; do not reintroduce without an explicit semantic model for APP-frame ownership and reentrancy boundaries.

